^SAMPLE = GSM4543826
!Sample_title = Treated with hydroxyurea 100 µM day 8 Nalm-6 screen
!Sample_geo_accession = GSM4543826
!Sample_status = Public on Aug 04 2020
!Sample_submission_date = May 11 2020
!Sample_last_update_date = Aug 04 2020
!Sample_type = SRA
!Sample_channel_count = 1
!Sample_source_name_ch1 = Treated with hydroxyurea 100 µM day 8 Nalm-6 screen
!Sample_organism_ch1 = Homo sapiens
!Sample_taxid_ch1 = 9606
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = cell line background: Nalm-6 pre-B lymphoid cell line
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = sample type: pooled sgRNA library
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = molecule subtype: sgRNAs PCR-amplified from genomic DNA
!Sample_treatment_protocol_ch1 = (NALM-6) A Nalm-6 clone with inducible expression of Cas9 was thawed, and Cas9 expression induced with doxycycline at 2 µg/mL for 8 days (see Bertomeu et al., 2018 for details). The pooled EKO library was split in different T-75 flasks and compounds were added (16 µM resveratrol, 16 µM pterostilbene, 100 µM hydroxyurea, or DMSO 0.1% v/v). Fresh media and compound was added at each cell passage.
!Sample_treatment_protocol_ch1 = (Jurkat) The genome-wide screen in Jurkat cells was performed by transduction of cells with the lentiviral TKOv3 library as described (Hart et al., 2017) with modifications as described. Cells were treated with 16 µM resveratrol or 0.1% DMSO v/v/ for 12 days. Fresh media and compound was added at each cell passage.
!Sample_growth_protocol_ch1 = Nalm-6 and Jurkat cells were grown in 10% FBS (v/v) (Wisent) RPMI 1640 medium (Wisent) at 5% (v/v) CO2 and 37°C.
!Sample_molecule_ch1 = genomic DNA
!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = Genomic DNA was extracted and purified using the Gentra Cell Puregene kit (QIAGEN, cat. # 158388).
!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = sgRNA libraries were prepared by PCR amplification to add sequencing adapters and indices followed by SPRI beads purification of sequencing-ready amplicons.
!Sample_description = processed data file: Nalm6_sgRNA_read_counts.txt
!Sample_data_processing = Reads were aligned using Bowtie2.2.5 in the forward direction only (--norc option) with otherwise default parameters and total read counts per sgRNA were tabulated.
!Sample_data_processing = Read counts from different sequencing lanes for the same sample were summed.
!Sample_data_processing = Read counts from all control samples and time-points from each experiment were summed.
!Sample_data_processing = Genome_build: For Nalm-6 screens: EKO sgRNA library (Bertomeu et al. 2017, PMID:29038160), using only the core gene-targting sgRNA set of of the library. For Jurkat screens: TKOv3 sgRNA library (Hart et al. 2017,PMID:28655737).
!Sample_data_processing = Supplementary_files_format_and_content: Tab-separated sgRNA read counts per sample
